  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Three Chanyu Gu Immortals gather above collapsing Imperial Court blessed land, with Chanyu Tong Zu as their leader. A young Gu Immortal says they hold the immortal killer move Winged Blade and can force a break in the wind veil of assimilation if they activate it together. Tong Zu warns that Hei Tribe, Ye Lui Tribe, Dong Fang Tribe, and other righteous path super tribes have sent Gu Immortals, and that Snowy Mountain has sent six, so the move must be timed against rivals as well as the veil.",
      "chapters": [
        635
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "winged-blade-at-the-wind-veil",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "loc_imperial_court_blessed_land",
        "move_winged_blade",
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "fac_ye_lui_tribe",
        "fac_dong_fang_tribe",
        "loc_snowy_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When they cut the veil, three Chanyu Gu Immortals appear in the sky breathing roughly after using Winged Blade.",
      "chapters": [
        636
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "winged-blade-at-the-wind-veil",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "As the tear closes in about eight breaths, other Gu Immortals urge the three Chanyu immortals to strike again. Tong Zu leads them, but they do not use Winged Blade a second time. The move costs heavy immortal essence, and they keep it ready to intimidate enemies in the chaotic fight.",
      "chapters": [
        638
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "winged-blade-at-the-wind-veil",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tong Zu leads around ten Northern Plains righteous path Gu Immortals into Dong Fang tribe’s Jade Pool blessed land. When Dong Fang Chang Fan offers deductions in exchange for a protective alliance after his death, Chanyu tribe accepts the conditions first through Tong Zu.",
      "chapters": [
        657
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dong-fang-transaction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "loc_jade_pool_blessed_land",
        "char_dong_fang_chang_fan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At a later auction, Chanyu tribe remains among three super forces still bidding with Yuan tribe and Murong tribe after other major buyers drop out, then leaves the competition.",
      "chapters": [
        763
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "auction-competition",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_yuan_tribe",
        "fac_murong_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ambush over a sandalwood sacred elephant egg: Chanyu Zhong Er names Chanyu tribe as Huang Jin bloodline while confronting Hei Cheng, and He Lang Zi treats Winged Blade as the tribe’s known immortal killer move during that ambush.",
      "chapters": [
        764
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "auction-competition",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chanyu_zhong_er",
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline",
        "char_hei_cheng",
        "char_he_lang_zi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the blood battle martial competition assembly, Chanyu tribe appears with Liu tribe, Ye Lui tribe, Meng tribe, Yuan tribe, Nian Er tribe, Murong tribe, and Guan tribe among Huang Jin super forces with territory and influence.",
      "chapters": [
        1193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blood-battle-assembly",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_liu_tribe",
        "fac_meng_tribe",
        "fac_nian_er_tribe",
        "fac_guan_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a clash involving the ancient battle formation Seven Extreme Desolation, Chanyu tribe’s Winged Blade sits beside Ye Lui tribe’s immortal binding rope as trump cards of their respective Huang Jin tribes.",
      "chapters": [
        1723
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blood-battle-assembly",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_seven_extreme_desolation"
      ]
    }
  ],
